menu "BLE Trigger Capability Configuration"

config CLAW_CAP_BLE_TRIGGER_ENABLED
    bool "Enable BLE Trigger Capability"
    default n
    depends on CLAW_CAP_VOICE_PIPELINE_ENABLED
    help
        Wireless push-to-talk: a remote BLE press starts voice capture and the
        matching release stops it, exactly as the on-board button does.

        Two sources feed the same trigger, and both can run at once:

          * A GATT service this device advertises. Any BLE debugging app can
            connect and write the trigger byte, which makes a phone usable as
            the button and is the only way to exercise this without hardware.

          * A BLE HID button (HOGP, service 0x1812) this device connects out
            to, for a real physical remote.

        Requires NimBLE with the central and observer roles enabled. This
        capability owns the NimBLE stack, so it cannot run alongside the `ble`
        or `ble_hid` Lua modules, which each own the stack themselves.

if CLAW_CAP_BLE_TRIGGER_ENABLED

config CLAW_CAP_BLE_TRIGGER_DEVICE_NAME
    string "Advertised device name"
    default "esp-claw-mic"
    help
        Name shown in the scan list of the phone app that connects to write
        the trigger byte.

config CLAW_CAP_BLE_TRIGGER_ADVERTISE
    bool "Advertise the trigger GATT service"
    default y
    help
        Turn off once a physical HID button is in use and no phone needs to
        connect, to stop advertising and free the connection slot.

config CLAW_CAP_BLE_TRIGGER_HID_HOST
    bool "Connect to BLE HID buttons"
    default y
    help
        Scan for peripherals advertising the HID service (0x1812) and treat
        their input reports as button presses.

config CLAW_CAP_BLE_TRIGGER_HID_SCAN_SEC
    int "HID scan window (seconds)"
    default 8
    range 2 30
    depends on CLAW_CAP_BLE_TRIGGER_HID_HOST
    help
        How long one scan runs. Scanning competes with Wi-Fi for the radio, so
        this never runs on a timer: it happens at startup and whenever
        ble_trigger_scan is called.

config CLAW_CAP_BLE_TRIGGER_HOLD_TIMEOUT_MS
    int "Maximum hold time (milliseconds)"
    default 15000
    range 1000 60000
    help
        A press with no matching release stops capture anyway after this long.
        Without it a dropped link mid-press would leave the microphone open
        until the recording cap expires.

endif

endmenu
